WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.640 --> 00:00:05.050
Speaker 1: We have been increasingly concerned
with what's going on with abortion rights

00:00:05.050 --> 00:00:07.259
in the United States.

00:00:07.259 --> 00:00:14.750
And the message that I had when Donald Trump
became president and started selecting people

00:00:14.750 --> 00:00:18.150
to the Supreme Court was they're not giving
up.

00:00:18.150 --> 00:00:19.160
They're going to try.

00:00:19.160 --> 00:00:23.749
They're going to do everything they can to
make abortion illegal.

00:00:23.749 --> 00:00:26.189
And they're going to do it by appealing cases
to the Supreme Court.

00:00:26.189 --> 00:00:30.730
And they did it, and we are now waiting to
see what the Supreme Court decides.

00:00:30.730 --> 00:00:35.100
But in the meantime, states aren't wasting
any time.

00:00:35.100 --> 00:00:41.219
Oklahoma Republicans have passed a law forcing
a woman to have her rapist's baby.

00:00:41.219 --> 00:00:47.440
It is a near-total ban on abortion, with no
exceptions for rape or incest.

00:00:47.440 --> 00:00:48.670
This isn't going to stop.

00:00:48.670 --> 00:00:51.540
They're going to keep doing it.

00:00:51.540 --> 00:00:59.460
Gov. Kevin's tit, who's the governor of Oklahoma,
says as governor, I represent all four million

00:00:59.460 --> 00:01:03.129
Oklahomans and they overwhelmingly support
protecting life.

00:01:03.129 --> 00:01:06.229
We want Oklahoma to be the most pro-life state
in the country.

00:01:06.229 --> 00:01:10.310
We want to outlaw abortion in the state of
Oklahoma.

00:01:10.310 --> 00:01:12.340
They're not kidding around.

00:01:12.340 --> 00:01:17.390
The bill also says anyone found guilty of
an abortion.

00:01:17.390 --> 00:01:21.939
Think about the language, Gill, if you're
found guilty of an abortion, you can get up

00:01:21.939 --> 00:01:26.799
to 10 years in jail and a $100000 fine.

00:01:26.799 --> 00:01:31.759
There are cases where convicted rapists don't
get 10 years in jail.

00:01:31.759 --> 00:01:33.600
And a $100000 fine.

00:01:33.600 --> 00:01:36.360
Some got only a few months jail time.

00:01:36.360 --> 00:01:44.880
And Oklahoma Governor Stitt signed the legislation
and it nearly bans all abortions in Oklahoma.

00:01:44.880 --> 00:01:46.780
The only exception left.

00:01:46.780 --> 00:01:54.360
The only carved out exception left is to save
the life of a pregnant woman in a medical

00:01:54.360 --> 00:01:55.360
emergency.

00:01:55.360 --> 00:02:00.689
And, of course, who gets to decide what such
a medical emergency is now.

00:02:00.689 --> 00:02:08.090
One of the odd things about this new law is
that Oklahoma already has a law on the books

00:02:08.090 --> 00:02:13.540
banning all abortions, except when necessary
to preserve the life of the pregnant person.

00:02:13.540 --> 00:02:17.260
The old law only has a five year prison sentence.

00:02:17.260 --> 00:02:22.760
The new law ups the maximum to 10 years and
$100000, so it's not even.

00:02:22.760 --> 00:02:26.310
We have no law and we are anti-abortion, so
let's pass a law.

00:02:26.310 --> 00:02:27.540
No, no, no, no, no.

00:02:27.540 --> 00:02:28.540
It's.

00:02:28.540 --> 00:02:29.540
We already have a law.

00:02:29.540 --> 00:02:30.540
We just don't think the punishment is strict
enough.

00:02:30.540 --> 00:02:32.599
So let's pass another law.

00:02:32.599 --> 00:02:37.129
It's become a race to the bottom with these
Republican culture wars, and we could all

00:02:37.129 --> 00:02:38.129
be living.

00:02:38.129 --> 00:02:43.900
I mean, modern technology and medicine and
innovation would allow us to be living in

00:02:43.900 --> 00:02:50.690
an age sort of sort of led by science and
enlightenment.

00:02:50.690 --> 00:02:58.690
But we are fighting a group of people that
is determined to have a country based on extreme

00:02:58.690 --> 00:03:00.970
Christian fundamentalism.

00:03:00.970 --> 00:03:05.190
And many of these Republicans, when you talk
to them.

00:03:05.190 --> 00:03:08.069
They're anti-abortion stance is based on a
religious belief.

00:03:08.069 --> 00:03:10.989
It's not a science based belief, it's a religious
belief.

00:03:10.989 --> 00:03:14.580
Now, strictly speaking, we have separation
of church and state.

00:03:14.580 --> 00:03:20.340
Formally, you're not supposed to be able to
justify a law with religious doctrine.

00:03:20.340 --> 00:03:25.080
In other words, it can't be written in the
law that because of what the Bible says, abortion

00:03:25.080 --> 00:03:26.450
is illegal.

00:03:26.450 --> 00:03:31.379
But all of these Republicans are using the
Bible to justify their votes, for sure.

00:03:31.379 --> 00:03:33.180
I'm not saying there's any way to prevent
that.

00:03:33.180 --> 00:03:38.250
I mean, you get into some really dicey First
Amendment issues, but understand that we have

00:03:38.250 --> 00:03:44.270
plenty of law in this country that is based
on the religious beliefs of the elected officials,

00:03:44.270 --> 00:03:47.100
and they're entitled to those beliefs, for
sure.

00:03:47.100 --> 00:03:54.770
But strictly speaking, officially, those beliefs
can't be the state's justification for a law.

00:03:54.770 --> 00:04:01.590
And again, I'm not saying that the free exercise
of religion should be suppressed, but religion

00:04:01.590 --> 00:04:05.159
is being used at the individual level to get
all of this stuff done.

00:04:05.159 --> 00:04:06.959
Now there's an important upcoming event.

00:04:06.959 --> 00:04:08.820
It is very plausible.

00:04:08.820 --> 00:04:09.820
I don't know.

00:04:09.820 --> 00:04:10.820
I don't know that I want to call it likely.

00:04:10.820 --> 00:04:12.300
I want to maintain some optimism.

00:04:12.300 --> 00:04:17.750
But it is possible that Roe v. Wade is in
its final days because we are expecting a

00:04:17.750 --> 00:04:20.520
decision in late June from the Supreme Court.

00:04:20.520 --> 00:04:26.610
Last December, the Supreme Court heard arguments
in Dobbs v. Jacobson Women's Health.

00:04:26.610 --> 00:04:30.670
Sorry, Dobbs v. Jackson Women's Health Organization.

00:04:30.670 --> 00:04:36.120
This is a Mississippi case, and it's asking
the court to overturn Roe v. Wade.

00:04:36.120 --> 00:04:41.280
And there are six justices currently on the
court who are at least open to overturning

00:04:41.280 --> 00:04:42.280
Roe v. Wade.

00:04:42.280 --> 00:04:44.330
Some of them are eager to do so.

00:04:44.330 --> 00:04:48.140
Twenty two states already have abortion bans
on the books.

00:04:48.140 --> 00:04:53.590
And so if Roe v. Wade is effectively overturned
by the forthcoming Supreme Court decision,

00:04:53.590 --> 00:05:00.360
those 22 states already have laws that basically
ban all abortions, and most of those would

00:05:00.360 --> 00:05:03.080
take effect immediately if Roe v. Wade is
overturned.

00:05:03.080 --> 00:05:11.790
A fascinating but grim reality is that some
of those abortion bans in certain states.

00:05:11.790 --> 00:05:13.630
Predate Roe v. Wade.

00:05:13.630 --> 00:05:19.190
They are really archaic, and those are the
anti-abortion laws that that would immediately

00:05:19.190 --> 00:05:23.550
be in play if Roe v. Wade is overturned in
late June by the Supreme Court.

00:05:23.550 --> 00:05:29.250
So the framework is already there, and we
could be seeing the United States rapidly

00:05:29.250 --> 00:05:36.780
accelerate to a sort of sci fi dystopian situation
with a resurgence of sort of back alley slash

00:05:36.780 --> 00:05:42.530
underground abortion clinics, people leaving
states in order to get the services they need

00:05:42.530 --> 00:05:43.750
elsewhere.

00:05:43.750 --> 00:05:45.100
You know, I often say we do.

00:05:45.100 --> 00:05:49.280
We don't want to point to a slippery slope
when there is unlikely to actually be one.

00:05:49.280 --> 00:05:51.530
We don't want to unnecessarily fearmonger.

00:05:51.530 --> 00:05:54.160
That's a tool of the reactionary, right?

00:05:54.160 --> 00:05:57.680
This is a very real possibility that we are
now facing.

00:05:57.680 --> 00:06:07.430
And Wisconsin's law makes abortion a felony
punishable by up to six years in prison.

00:06:07.430 --> 00:06:11.310
That law is over 100 years old.

00:06:11.310 --> 00:06:17.170
And it's not likely to be repealed, meaning
if Roe v. Wade is overturned, that's the Wisconsin

00:06:17.170 --> 00:06:18.640
law that goes into place.

00:06:18.640 --> 00:06:21.840
It's not been relevant because of Roe v. Wade.

00:06:21.840 --> 00:06:22.840
Scary times ahead.

00:06:22.840 --> 00:06:24.560
Very, very scary times ahead.

